WEBVTT

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:23.520
Sociedade Custou, Turner and Amaya Filmes present

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:29.910
A story raised in strong memories

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:47.360
For those from far away, sent here, it was known as the Vietnam War.

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:51.230
Here, it was known as the American War.

00:01:59.020 --> 00:01:59.620
Ordinary people,

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.440
in search of their daily subsistence in the river and in the fields,

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:06.560
were caught in the crossfire of a political fury.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:28.510
A poison storm came down from the sky over the small country.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.060
with a greater amount of bombs than the ones thrown in World War II.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:51.390
And when it was over, with bare hands and tools of antiquity,

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:56.410
ordinary people began to rebuild their world and their way of life.

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:08.650
The soldier's day is over. The peasant's day is back.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:18.180
Today, a happy Vietnam works with simple means towards a dream of prosperity.

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:25.380
However, not everything can be completely redone.

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:29.080
The poison storm remains in the soils and in the bodies.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.780
still causing birth defects, cancers, abortions.

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:42.220
The boy is two years old, born without limbs,

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:47.670
apparently due to the genetic cruelty of dioxin, a chemical dewormer.

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:53.480
Within the animated spirit of his culture, he apologizes to Anne Marie Cousteau.

00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:56.650
I would smile at you, but now I'm eating rice.

00:03:57.150 --> 00:03:59.630
Four million died...

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.740
or were wounded during the war, and for some, the difficulty continues,

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:06.030
but peace offers hope.

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:11.270
However, in neighboring Cambodia, the war persists,

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:12.710
bombs still disfigure,

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:16.020
and peace is something as uncertain as a game of chance.

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:21.160
To understand two such contrasting lands,

00:04:21.430 --> 00:04:23.990
Jean-Michel Cousteau will lead an expedition

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:27.270
on the channel that connects them and traces their destinies,

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:29.970
the Mekong River.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:38.940
Throughout its margins, through time, an ancient people has been abhorred by sadness,

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:46.300
but, however, marked by perseverance, always looking forward with the young face of hope.

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:52.560
Vietnam and Cambodia, children of rice and weapons.

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:04.820
It cost Rediscover the World.

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:57.540
After the Eucalyptus, the Earth team led by Jean-Michel Cousteau enters a world where the serenity of the forest and the river can be illusory.

00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:09.640
After following the central Mekong through quiet isolation in Laos and Thailand,

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:15.440
they approach the region where the Great River became a symbol of international conflict.

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:21.730
The Mekong, the largest river in Southeast Asia, begins in the Himalayas,

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:27.170
then passing, with increasing volume, through six countries to the South China Sea.

00:06:27.250 --> 00:06:29.980
The Calypso will navigate to the north since...

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.580
from the river in Vietnam, to find the land team

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:36.280
that now crosses southwards into Cambodia.

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:43.150
The timeless nature of life in the river, the daily panorama,

00:06:43.530 --> 00:06:45.250
the plantation and the fishing,

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:48.070
seem identical to what was observed above the river.

00:06:51.900 --> 00:06:54.660
But just a few kilometers after the border,

00:06:54.940 --> 00:06:57.520
among the people busy with innocent tasks,

00:06:57.620 --> 00:06:59.110
the team finds the unexpected.

00:07:02.970 --> 00:07:04.010
Up there, on the right.

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:08.270
The shot that went through the bow came as a warning.

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:11.930
We showed our willingness to collaborate.

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:18.250
The borders of the Mekong in Cambodia are burning with political stability.

00:07:18.390 --> 00:07:23.200
Four different armed groups competing for national power.

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:26.540
Our interrogators are government soldiers.

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:28.020
Almost all of them are teenagers.

00:07:28.020 --> 00:07:29.970
Even so, Carreiro...

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:32.740
with automatic weapons and with the authority to use them.

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:34.720
I show my passport.

00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:43.090
One of the young men has enough ammunition to sink the Calypso.

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:44.900
It's true.

00:07:46.140 --> 00:07:52.320
Thank you very much.

00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:52.860
Okay?

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:55.870
Okay.

00:07:56.170 --> 00:07:56.610
Thank you.

00:07:56.670 --> 00:07:57.630
Thank you.

00:08:01.310 --> 00:08:01.870
Thank you.

00:08:02.720 --> 00:08:04.440
Well, what was that about?

00:08:04.660 --> 00:08:05.540
It's just a checkpoint.

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:09.020
You know, we've gone through the border and...

00:08:09.020 --> 00:08:11.430
It's a scary way to say it.

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:15.380
To be checked, but I think it will be fine.

00:08:15.780 --> 00:08:18.000
We are officially in Cambodia now.

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:18.520
Welcome.

00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:25.750
The violence of the ongoing conflict is so much after decades of civil war

00:08:25.750 --> 00:08:29.970
that for many years the United Nations has its greatest strength...

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.300
of peace anchored in Cambodia.

00:08:31.660 --> 00:08:36.660
When they find a US patrol boat,

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:39.920
the crew asks about the risks of sailing in the river.

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:46.200
If you are stopped, the only ones who will do it

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:49.460
will be people like us to ask what you are doing.

00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:52.000
Okay, we don't have any problems with that.

00:08:52.280 --> 00:08:55.420
A soldier tells us that in a nation with little money

00:08:55.420 --> 00:08:58.780
to pay its armies, even the government troops

00:08:58.780 --> 00:08:59.960
for some sailors in the river

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:01.100
and take your money.

00:09:01.380 --> 00:09:02.860
You mean government soldiers?

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:05.610
Yes, government soldiers.

00:09:08.670 --> 00:09:12.130
A radio communication with the leader of the Earth Exploration Team,

00:09:12.630 --> 00:09:15.150
Don Santee, and the Calypso crew,

00:09:15.170 --> 00:09:17.790
now approaching the Mekong Delta in Vietnam,

00:09:18.110 --> 00:09:21.810
are eager to get to the safety of their comrades in Cambodia.

00:09:23.470 --> 00:09:26.190
The ship's expedition leader, Bertrand Sion,

00:09:26.410 --> 00:09:29.850
reports that on his journey towards the reunion of the...

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:34.600
in Cambodia, the Calypso will explore the canals and arms that cross the flat

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:46.400
Delta expansion. As soon as the Vietnam flag is hoisted, a boat from the team

00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:50.470
goes out to witness a rare oceanic harvest, called

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:51.650
sand skating.

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:21.670
During the lowest tides of each year,

00:10:21.810 --> 00:10:24.760
families sweep the coast of Bahia

00:10:24.760 --> 00:10:28.920
sliding on wooden boards in search of edible treasures.

00:10:37.020 --> 00:10:41.940
For the Calypso team, the collection of seafood and shrimp mantis

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:46.600
illustrates the fertile impact of Mekong in the sea and the initiative of the Vietnamese.

00:10:47.240 --> 00:10:59.680
Without any modern technology, the Vietnamese depend on their number of inhabitants

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.460
and their ancestral knowledge of nature

00:11:02.820 --> 00:11:05.220
to gather and use everything it provides.

00:11:05.800 --> 00:11:11.080
For navigator Thierry Stern,

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:14.350
the scene also reveals a contagious spirit

00:11:14.350 --> 00:11:17.740
that for a long time has relieved the hardships of work and war.

00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:26.660
For Calypso, the low tide means maneuvering between shallow margins

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:29.460
and strong currents to enter the Mekong.

00:11:31.320 --> 00:11:37.480
Local pilots from the river help with instructions, but communication is as difficult as navigation.

00:11:38.200 --> 00:11:50.860
About 80 kilometers inland, in Kantô, the task is not navigation, but diplomacy.

00:11:51.580 --> 00:11:57.480
The inhabitants of the most important city in the Delta gathered to receive the ship and its crew,

00:11:57.920 --> 00:11:59.960
led in this mission by the captain.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:01.980
by Captain Christophe Chouette-Pastray.

00:12:10.980 --> 00:12:18.200
Despite being one of the largest stages of the Vietnam War

00:12:18.200 --> 00:12:19.780
and the communist fortress,

00:12:19.900 --> 00:12:22.800
the Delta seems surprisingly remote today.

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:27.440
The visit of a famous research vessel is a rare occasion,

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:29.840
an opportunity for music and games.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:34.920
to bring shared laughter between people who were already mortal enemies.

00:12:35.180 --> 00:12:51.320
Yes, in animation and irony, Calypso heads to the great Mekong.

00:12:51.460 --> 00:12:59.970
At Mekong, in Vietnam, Calypso meets...

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.600
a world flooded by recent history,

00:13:02.600 --> 00:13:05.600
but little altered by modern development.

00:13:07.196 --> 00:13:09.696
No great bridge crosses the Mekong.

00:13:10.428 --> 00:13:14.848
Only ferryboats cross this 12th longest river in the world.

00:13:21.948 --> 00:13:24.128
Along its margins in the Delta,

00:13:24.128 --> 00:13:26.628
All existence seems to be linked to water.

00:13:27.068 --> 00:13:29.068
Humanity here is amphibious.

00:13:30.570 --> 00:13:35.210
Time and habits produced a lifestyle especially adapted to the water.

00:13:36.720 --> 00:13:43.380
The abundant margins also reflect the explosive population growth

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:49.780
and the need for work is constant in a land where the average income is US$ 200 per year.

00:14:06.652 --> 00:14:12.472
With limited space and money, many families became completely aquatic.

00:14:12.604 --> 00:14:15.604
even getting to live in the river in boat houses.

00:14:15.868 --> 00:14:19.428
taking almost all aspects of life, floating.

00:14:19.676 --> 00:14:21.676
little by little, stepping on the ground.

00:14:28.892 --> 00:14:29.972
...creating fish in...

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:33.220
people look for free protein in Rio,

00:14:33.520 --> 00:14:34.720
that they can barely afford.

00:14:35.300 --> 00:14:44.980
There is an industry aligned on the margins of the river.

00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:46.520
of the river and the canals.

00:14:46.620 --> 00:14:48.900
But as Captain Eucalyptus sees,

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:52.080
they are mostly moved by human energy.

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:54.200
The factory is partially floating.

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:58.040
The equipment is a matter of smart resources,

00:14:58.500 --> 00:14:59.320
not machinery.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:01.000
elaborated

00:15:03.548 --> 00:15:06.548
Subtitles by the Amara.org community

00:15:09.116 --> 00:15:13.116
Typically, the most modern equipment is a manual tool.

00:15:13.244 --> 00:15:15.644
the gravity transport system.

00:15:18.012 --> 00:15:21.652
In the aquatic world, agriculture does not limit itself to land.

00:15:21.724 --> 00:15:24.724
and the creations are made in extensions on the water.

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:35.120
The happy life of newlyweds starts in Rio.

00:15:38.348 --> 00:15:40.108
And life ends here too.

00:15:40.140 --> 00:15:43.220
in the sadness of a floating funeral procession.

00:15:47.884 --> 00:15:50.024
On the crossing of the Delta canals,

00:15:50.220 --> 00:15:54.220
Villages exist almost exclusively as shopping centers

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:59.220
for the purchase, exchange and export of products from neighboring fields.

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:02.060
And like almost everything else in the Delta,

00:16:02.428 --> 00:16:05.268
the competing markets are floating.

00:16:32.400 --> 00:16:34.380
On this day, there are, among the buyers,

00:16:34.900 --> 00:16:40.220
visitors coming from afar, curious to taste the flavors and fragrances of an exotic world.

00:16:53.720 --> 00:16:54.300
Here,

00:17:00.092 --> 00:17:02.092
The same fun is made in the water.

00:17:02.972 --> 00:17:07.732
Custod's crew board a boat that travels from one town to another.

00:17:07.772 --> 00:17:09.772
with the stage and musicians.

00:17:22.652 --> 00:17:26.652
The songs reflect the permanence of the foreigners who passed through here.

00:17:27.292 --> 00:17:29.992
In an old Vietnamese stage, a music show

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:31.760
and pop music with an American influence.

00:17:37.560 --> 00:17:44.900
When the show ends, the stage and the stage are folded

00:17:44.900 --> 00:17:47.940
and the entire theater departs for the next show.

00:18:00.764 --> 00:18:05.564
Among the markets, the team finds live products from nature.

00:18:10.428 --> 00:18:13.428
Monkeys are sold as animals of esteem.

00:18:13.660 --> 00:18:17.980
But where the flesh is scarce, the snake is seen not as a demon,

00:18:18.076 --> 00:18:20.076
but as an iguaria.

00:18:23.068 --> 00:18:26.508
The abundance of poisonous snakes in this tropical land

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:28.920
attracts the interest of the on-board doctor

00:18:28.956 --> 00:18:29.996
Denis Martin Laval

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:32.100
responsible for the safety of the crew.

00:18:33.580 --> 00:18:37.840
Investigar, he accompanies the team to a farm in the Delta that breeds poisonous snakes.

00:18:38.160 --> 00:18:48.060
He is surprised by the carefree attitude of the natives in relation to safety.

00:18:52.390 --> 00:18:56.930
Anaja, armed with a poison that can paralyze the human nervous system.

00:19:07.360 --> 00:19:08.100
According to tradition,

00:19:08.620 --> 00:19:12.120
nages and other poisonous snakes are created by their venom,

00:19:12.440 --> 00:19:14.600
which is extracted for medicinal purposes.

00:19:22.130 --> 00:19:25.870
The lethal fluid is transformed into a remedy for rheumatism and insomnia.

00:19:26.010 --> 00:19:28.100
It is even used as a cough sedative.

00:19:32.780 --> 00:19:36.240
For financial gain, the serum for the snakebite is exported,

00:19:36.770 --> 00:19:40.510
while locally people are treated with medicinal herbs.

00:19:40.790 --> 00:19:48.320
The girl in the farm's medical center was bitten in the foot.

00:19:48.760 --> 00:19:51.340
Without treatment, she could die of hemorrhage.

00:19:56.810 --> 00:19:59.970
Dr. Martin Laval is informed...

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:04.280
It is known that the marks on the teeth reveal that the snake was an arboreal viper.

00:20:04.412 --> 00:20:08.172
who probably found the girl while she was hunting for frogs on the ground.

00:20:13.308 --> 00:20:19.308
Every year, about 400 victims of snake bites visit the center for a traditional cure.

00:20:19.356 --> 00:20:21.956
All but 1% survive.

00:20:22.300 --> 00:20:27.300
The team is informed that in two days the girl was already out of danger and walking.

00:20:31.084 --> 00:20:33.924
In Sok Trang Village, south of the Delta,

00:20:33.996 --> 00:20:39.316
Dr. Martão Laval and Sion examine the traditional drugs sold by camelos.

00:20:39.564 --> 00:20:44.004
and then visit a different medical clinic, installed in a pagoda.

00:20:44.620 --> 00:20:51.220
The scene is another proof that most people in the Delta still believe in the old ways and old curses.

00:20:57.740 --> 00:20:59.980
Ancient medical treatments are the first...

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:04.800
first prepared by voluntary ancients, well versed in the art of native healing.

00:21:06.870 --> 00:21:19.360
Workers follow the pharmacopoeia that dates from the first Chinese occupations

00:21:19.360 --> 00:21:22.720
and knowledge recorded 600 years ago.

00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:25.080
Science comes from ancient times.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:33.000
and their ancestors, the ingredients of nature.

00:21:39.220 --> 00:21:44.320
In the Pagode's antechamber, the patients are examined by specialists

00:21:44.320 --> 00:21:48.800
called healers, who make their diagnoses behind a table

00:21:48.800 --> 00:21:52.760
and prescribe herbal medicines for diseases or revigorants.

00:21:53.020 --> 00:21:57.280
The medicines are free, despite many making donations.

00:21:57.940 --> 00:21:59.520
The prescriptions are filled

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:01.020
by Western pharmacists,

00:22:01.880 --> 00:22:04.880
who mix substances such as elephant grass root,

00:22:05.000 --> 00:22:08.000
tangerine peel, cinnamon, chrysanthemum,

00:22:08.260 --> 00:22:10.760
frog skin and veal horn.

00:22:11.500 --> 00:22:15.490
Here, ancient medicines are more reliable

00:22:15.490 --> 00:22:16.770
than Western drugs.

00:22:16.930 --> 00:22:20.580
And there is another benefit, they are accessible.

00:22:25.610 --> 00:22:27.330
Through the Mekong Delta,

00:22:27.370 --> 00:22:29.860
human naivety subjugated society.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:38.310
forces of nature. A vast network of channels and water sources distributes the water from the river,

00:22:38.450 --> 00:22:44.100
limiting the destructive incursion of salty water and the periodic floods that can flood

00:22:44.100 --> 00:22:50.470
the land more than one arm above sea level. Longer than Mekong itself, the system of

00:22:50.470 --> 00:22:55.930
channels transforms the previously desolate land into a forest of fruit and coconut forests,

00:22:56.180 --> 00:22:58.220
surrounded by immense rice fields.

00:23:09.310 --> 00:23:17.860
Enriched and irrigated by Mekong, the rice fields through the Delta have helped Vietnam to be the third world rice exporter.

00:23:24.540 --> 00:23:29.690
Encouraged by such success, the Vietnamese plan new irrigation projects

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:33.500
to expand their harvests, stimulating the national recovery

00:23:33.500 --> 00:23:36.580
in fields that were already devastated by the war.

00:23:36.820 --> 00:23:43.080
With the effort of human labor and the perfect management of the soil,

00:23:43.320 --> 00:23:47.030
Vietnam progresses like a boat full of rice and optimism.

00:23:47.290 --> 00:23:57.930
In Cambodia, however,

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:02.380
We live in a world with a lack of optimism.

00:24:02.820 --> 00:24:08.620
In a land also blessed by the fertility of the Mekong,

00:24:09.460 --> 00:24:12.670
peace and prosperity escape from the peasants.

00:24:12.890 --> 00:24:17.100
And decades of war have made the rice fields

00:24:17.100 --> 00:24:19.280
a place of danger always present

00:24:19.280 --> 00:24:22.650
for workers and unnoticed children.

00:24:31.180 --> 00:24:34.160
It is estimated that there are about 4 million mines

00:24:34.160 --> 00:24:37.080
buried in Leo, in western Cambodia,

00:24:37.080 --> 00:24:39.660
by troops and terrorists,

00:24:40.020 --> 00:24:43.560
even by loggers desperate to defend their fields.

00:24:43.780 --> 00:24:48.260
In the effort, which seems useless,

00:24:48.460 --> 00:24:50.100
to find so many traps,

00:24:50.700 --> 00:24:53.640
specialists in disarming United Nations mines

00:24:53.640 --> 00:24:56.210
risk their own lives and members.

00:25:22.780 --> 00:25:25.660
he finds a mine that serves a diabolical purpose,

00:25:26.140 --> 00:25:28.910
to mutilate more than to kill.

00:25:30.030 --> 00:25:31.990
retarding a troop with the load of wounded.

00:25:32.350 --> 00:25:35.280
But the mines mutilate the innocent,

00:25:35.740 --> 00:25:37.810
long after the fight ends.

00:25:39.960 --> 00:25:43.800
A specialist says that the mines are hard to find

00:25:44.220 --> 00:25:46.740
because they migrate on the soil of flooded fields.

00:25:47.560 --> 00:25:51.550
Therefore, children will still be wounded in the years to come.

00:25:53.280 --> 00:25:53.580
Today,

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:04.760
Camboja has more defective people per capita than any other nation in the world.

00:26:33.660 --> 00:26:39.180
The Director of the Rehabilitation Center says that there are 20,000 amputated in Cambodia

00:26:40.160 --> 00:26:42.680
and 200 new cases per month.

00:26:43.940 --> 00:26:45.980
Some estimates are higher.

00:26:47.180 --> 00:26:51.740
And it seems that as 10,000 die without receiving medical treatment.

00:26:51.900 --> 00:26:56.880
It's a sad scenario.

00:26:56.880 --> 00:26:59.600
children to work,

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:04.780
or play innocently in a field and suddenly find themselves

00:27:04.780 --> 00:27:08.520
traumatically disfigured, equipped, if they are lucky,

00:27:08.800 --> 00:27:11.960
with an artificial member that offers them the chance

00:27:11.960 --> 00:27:13.360
to adjust to society.

00:27:13.860 --> 00:27:16.900
The amputated without prosthesis have as a future

00:27:16.900 --> 00:27:18.420
a life of beggars.

00:27:18.540 --> 00:27:27.220
Just like their children, Camboja seems to have

00:27:27.220 --> 00:27:29.320
its natural potential unjustly denied.

00:27:30.090 --> 00:27:32.870
by dismantling forces of a political chaos.

00:27:32.990 --> 00:27:38.300
Even so, in the distant gaze of a boy,

00:27:38.480 --> 00:27:41.320
I see the hope of his people.

00:27:41.880 --> 00:27:44.820
He does not know if he will walk again,

00:27:45.480 --> 00:27:49.220
but he insists that he will be an electronic technician.

00:27:49.440 --> 00:27:53.820
For now, Cambodians have small dreams,

00:27:54.040 --> 00:27:58.390
dreams of safety, of being normal.

00:28:02.780 --> 00:28:05.880
Few natural extensions that were visited by the Calypso

00:28:05.880 --> 00:28:10.220
seem so greatly manipulated and explored for human needs

00:28:10.220 --> 00:28:14.270
as the Mekong Delta, considering, for example, the coconut.

00:28:21.050 --> 00:28:25.630
In the forced austerity of post-war, the Vietnamese do not waste anything.

00:28:26.830 --> 00:28:29.970
Even the empty shells are burned in ovens to...

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:32.900
for the export as raw material of carbon filters,

00:28:32.900 --> 00:28:35.390
for drinking water, aquariums,

00:28:35.390 --> 00:28:40.530
even protective suits used in nuclear plants in Europe and Asia.

00:28:43.330 --> 00:28:46.850
Through a province of the South densely occupied by coconut trees,

00:28:47.050 --> 00:28:50.650
the team finds small factories moved by human labor,

00:28:50.650 --> 00:28:52.590
turning coconuts into products.

00:28:52.910 --> 00:28:59.980
The apparent...

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:04.400
This unusable external fiber will be transformed into carpet in another place.

00:29:04.660 --> 00:29:13.390
More conventional, the pulp and the oil are processed in various edible products.

00:29:13.530 --> 00:29:20.140
However, during the war, in the lack of fuel, the Vietnamese even burned coconut oil in lamps.

00:29:20.760 --> 00:29:29.500
Today, the most appreciated product is the sweet, prepared in kitchens full of women, without any modern equipment.

00:29:32.490 --> 00:29:41.040
wrapped by girls who, in a richer country, would only eat it.

00:29:41.240 --> 00:29:45.710
All this is derived, with ingenuity,

00:29:45.910 --> 00:29:49.530
from a tree that also provides leaves for baskets and covers,

00:29:50.010 --> 00:29:53.350
and daily drink and food for the peasants themselves.

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:02.720
Since the candy is acquired when visiting the village,

00:30:03.040 --> 00:30:07.560
most Vietnamese families only allow these guloseimas sporadically,

00:30:07.880 --> 00:30:10.620
leading to a life of Spartan simplicity.

00:30:10.680 --> 00:30:19.260
For the Nguyen family, tomorrow in the market is followed by a taxi trip back home.

00:30:19.580 --> 00:30:29.980
As well as 85% of Vietnamese, they live as countrymen.

00:30:30.660 --> 00:30:53.260
Father and son work together to generate the sustenance of the family,

00:30:53.520 --> 00:30:59.980
daily gathering coconuts in a profitable harvest of a land that they cannot own due to the laws of nature.

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:02.940
but for decades they have the right to exploit.

00:31:07.410 --> 00:31:12.550
The coconuts also supply houses without gas or electric current with fuel oil.

00:31:12.650 --> 00:31:19.630
In the absence of a refrigerator,

00:31:19.970 --> 00:31:24.890
a nearby tank keeps live and fresh fish cornered until necessary.

00:31:39.880 --> 00:31:43.420
As in all places, women carry out domestic tasks.

00:31:44.050 --> 00:31:48.830
Tradition and government policy encourage little extravagance in clothing and behavior,

00:31:49.250 --> 00:31:52.540
as well as the discipline of daily practice of the martial arts.

00:32:03.040 --> 00:32:15.520
The Nguyen people rely a lot on products made locally and live in a house made of real estate mostly with local materials.

00:32:15.880 --> 00:32:23.800
Spending nothing, recycling resources, they accept a modest but comfortable existence while waiting for a better future.

00:32:31.760 --> 00:32:36.500
As we saw in Cambodia, families also depend on the free products of nature.

00:32:38.840 --> 00:32:48.940
We are going on a fishing excursion, but in a dirty country with explosives, people recycle weapons.

00:33:00.380 --> 00:33:04.360
The idea is to kill fish, and the technique is effective.

00:33:04.820 --> 00:33:17.040
But because they use an easy way to collect food for the present,

00:33:17.360 --> 00:33:19.400
they stone their future.

00:33:22.330 --> 00:33:25.340
Only about 20% of the dead fish comes to the surface.

00:33:25.680 --> 00:33:27.260
The rest is wasted.

00:33:30.160 --> 00:33:32.860
As a result, in some parts of the Mekong in Cambodia,

00:33:33.180 --> 00:33:35.600
the fish collection fell by half.

00:33:40.440 --> 00:33:43.180
We witnessed a land polluted by war.

00:33:53.480 --> 00:33:56.100
On board the Calypso, on the way to Cambodia,

00:33:56.240 --> 00:33:57.260
a day of beauty.

00:34:08.730 --> 00:34:14.710
The crew is fighting against a temporary lethargy imposed by tropical heat for weeks.

00:34:26.760 --> 00:34:29.930
Usually welcome tasks are, if possible...

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:34.420
One believes to be the service of the other, which does not agree.

00:34:34.760 --> 00:34:39.360
There are also other impositions.

00:34:39.780 --> 00:34:42.440
Approaching the border between Vietnam and Cambodia,

00:34:42.720 --> 00:34:45.860
the ship is visited by Vietnamese border guards,

00:34:45.860 --> 00:34:51.700
who provide an apparently endless amount of authorizations, permissions and passports

00:34:51.700 --> 00:34:54.360
before authorizing the passage of the ship.

00:34:54.560 --> 00:34:58.540
The paperwork that took months to be obtained in two hours of checking.

00:35:00.800 --> 00:35:09.200
Almost immediately, the Vietnamese are replaced by their Cambodian colleagues,

00:35:09.200 --> 00:35:11.980
who meticulously study the same documents.

00:35:19.120 --> 00:35:21.640
Emerging from the Mekong as a warning signal,

00:35:21.760 --> 00:35:25.380
the shell of a cargo sunk by insurgent forces

00:35:25.380 --> 00:35:28.460
offers a new evidence of the proximity of Cambodia.

00:35:38.640 --> 00:35:40.860
In a remote area of the Mekong, in Cambodia,

00:35:41.240 --> 00:35:43.740
after months of separate journeys,

00:35:43.980 --> 00:35:47.740
old friends of the Earth team of Gusteau and Ducalypso

00:35:47.740 --> 00:35:48.980
approach the meeting.

00:36:23.100 --> 00:36:28.700
Jean-Michel's team traveled almost 1,600 kilometers from the central Mekong through four nations.

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:34.620
and his crew gather in the mother ship for a joint exploration of Cambodia.

00:36:44.720 --> 00:36:50.060
From the Calypso Helicopter, Felix, I see the sign of the sad state of destruction of Cambodia.

00:36:50.500 --> 00:36:57.800
The richest forests of the north are cut as if they were wood,

00:36:58.020 --> 00:36:59.920
and sent to large batches of machinery.

00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:09.280
Without management or replanting, enemy armies sell the trees to raise funds for armament.

00:37:13.080 --> 00:37:16.140
Here, the sorrows of nature and humanity mix.

00:37:16.740 --> 00:37:24.580
We are approaching the capital of Phnom Penh, which has already been the largest and most vibrant city in the Mekong region.

00:37:27.950 --> 00:37:29.800
Today, it is a disturbing sight.

00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:36.240
The Royal Palace is a reminder of a former elegance,

00:37:36.260 --> 00:37:41.080
before what the people of the countryside call a sour and bitter time.

00:37:42.960 --> 00:37:46.650
During the end of the 70s, the four-year-old Reynaldo de Meia-Rouge

00:37:46.960 --> 00:37:52.300
destroyed the fountain, leaving it rusted and littered to this day.

00:37:52.440 --> 00:37:59.560
The entire population of the capital was brutally evacuated to work in the fields.

00:38:00.990 --> 00:38:06.400
Almost half of the 7 million Cambodians died and the culture fell into disgrace.

00:38:06.740 --> 00:38:18.780
The hope was almost extinguished.

00:38:18.820 --> 00:38:27.280
But along the borders, we noticed a sign that the rebirth is on its way.

00:38:28.610 --> 00:38:29.550
The race on the ship...

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:33.220
seems marked by a reminiscent incitation of the past,

00:38:33.460 --> 00:38:36.380
before the genocide of Khmer Rouge

00:38:36.380 --> 00:38:38.510
and the incessant civil war that followed.

00:38:38.830 --> 00:38:46.470
Despite everything, the Cambodians seem determined to move forward

00:38:46.930 --> 00:38:48.660
with an obstinate spirit.

00:39:16.410 --> 00:39:22.870
As the emblem of a pacific past, the rhythm is given not by the screams of a reaper, but by a graceful woman.

00:40:08.410 --> 00:40:16.550
In the heart of the Cambodian culture, the eucalyptus sails an affluent of the Mekong to a vital organ of its environment, the Ton Nesap Lake,

00:40:16.570 --> 00:40:26.300
a huge natural reservoir that has its triplicated area in the rain season, receiving the vast flood of the Mekong and limiting the floods of the Delta.

00:40:27.830 --> 00:40:29.910
Along its edges, villages...

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:35.920
The flutters wander through the unstable margins, exploring one of the most rich reserves of freshwater fish.

00:40:36.060 --> 00:40:48.770
As it overflows every year, Tonner, Saab and Vahre Organic Materials create true culture fountains that provide an ideal incubator for young fish.

00:40:52.370 --> 00:40:56.590
Calypso enters while the aquatic region called the Great Lagoon is decreasing.

00:41:02.840 --> 00:41:07.960
Like a family island, a house-boat migrates to deeper waters.

00:41:08.120 --> 00:41:13.060
Part of a lifestyle dominated by fish and water,

00:41:13.160 --> 00:41:16.120
which is considered normal by the inhabitants of the village.

00:41:31.980 --> 00:41:35.360
Although part of the fishing is used for daily sustenance,

00:41:35.400 --> 00:41:38.840
the lake also supplies young fish for exportation.

00:41:41.150 --> 00:41:43.450
Maintained alive in mobile tanks,

00:41:43.590 --> 00:41:46.690
the fish are transported downstream to the Delta.

00:41:49.830 --> 00:41:53.300
Returning to Vietnam, the Calypso team examines a tank

00:41:53.300 --> 00:41:56.600
that is being built to house the fish that is about to arrive.

00:42:06.880 --> 00:42:13.400
The construction is another example of Vietnamese confidence in the power of muscle strength and manual tools.

00:42:21.400 --> 00:42:29.970
The team's interpreter, Hai Son, says that the structure will be submerged, and where they are stopped, 200 people will be killed.

00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:33.560
How many tons of fish will mature to a commercial size every year?

00:42:35.890 --> 00:42:39.770
A fish farm working reveals the efficiency of such an operation.

00:42:39.970 --> 00:42:46.590
On the submerged tank, operators prepare the fish feed

00:42:46.590 --> 00:42:49.620
made in its majority of pre-thrown materials,

00:42:49.840 --> 00:42:52.850
such as rice husks and peeled vegetables.

00:42:54.920 --> 00:42:59.980
15 tons of young fish will become 90 tons of fresh fish.

00:43:00.000 --> 00:43:00.540
of frozen fish.

00:43:01.580 --> 00:43:03.500
Jouet Pastret says to the owner,

00:43:03.680 --> 00:43:05.960
it will be possible to walk on the water.

00:43:08.010 --> 00:43:09.830
The mature fish is transferred alive

00:43:09.830 --> 00:43:11.820
in baskets made by hand

00:43:11.820 --> 00:43:13.140
from its aquatic corral,

00:43:13.140 --> 00:43:15.900
connected to a frozen fish factory.

00:43:16.020 --> 00:43:20.140
Thus, the fish will be exported

00:43:20.140 --> 00:43:21.680
like most of what is collected

00:43:21.680 --> 00:43:22.480
from the Vietnamese water and soil.

00:43:33.100 --> 00:43:33.620
That's all.

00:43:36.910 --> 00:43:40.340
They leave inside a transport boat,

00:43:40.360 --> 00:43:42.280
the equivalent of a cattle truck.

00:43:50.170 --> 00:43:51.430
Despite the good management,

00:43:52.010 --> 00:43:55.080
the people of the Delta face environmental problems.

00:43:55.700 --> 00:43:57.520
The fish from Lake Tonesap

00:43:57.520 --> 00:43:59.750
are being threatened by sediments

00:43:59.750 --> 00:43:59.970
that are not suitable for fishing.

00:44:00.000 --> 00:44:02.580
that falls into the lake due to the deforestation

00:44:02.580 --> 00:44:05.640
carried out by the rebel armies in the mountains of Cambodia.

00:44:05.980 --> 00:44:13.380
The calypso discovers, on its way back to the sea,

00:44:13.560 --> 00:44:16.670
that the mangroves in the delta canals are disappearing,

00:44:17.330 --> 00:44:20.970
torn apart to give way to shrimp farms.

00:44:24.090 --> 00:44:26.530
In its enthusiasm to develop agriculture

00:44:26.530 --> 00:44:29.390
as part of the national campaign for prosperity,

00:44:30.250 --> 00:44:35.190
the Vietnamese camponese ignore the life cycle of the creatures they depend on.

00:44:35.190 --> 00:44:39.490
The shrimp captured from the sea and grown in their tanks

00:44:39.490 --> 00:44:42.230
has started its life being fed and protected

00:44:42.230 --> 00:44:45.010
between the mangrove cut to breed the tanks.

00:44:46.870 --> 00:44:51.490
Ecologically, the camponese are eliminating the base on which they sustain themselves.

00:45:00.990 --> 00:45:04.650
The initial abundance of shrimp has supported not only the peasants,

00:45:04.770 --> 00:45:07.800
but an air-conditioning industry that employs thousands,

00:45:08.280 --> 00:45:11.900
and a favorable commercial market exporting frozen shrimp,

00:45:11.900 --> 00:45:13.440
largely to Japan.

00:45:13.840 --> 00:45:22.990
But while the manguezais shrink in a narrow belt at the ends of the farms in expansion,

00:45:23.390 --> 00:45:27.250
the concern that shrimp production also decreases.

00:45:31.440 --> 00:45:35.080
Therefore, today, the Vietnamese are replanting their vans,

00:45:36.710 --> 00:45:39.930
encouraging children to plant trees in quantity,

00:45:40.760 --> 00:45:43.020
rebuilding the past for their future.

00:45:46.160 --> 00:45:48.000
Few people know as well as Vietnamese

00:45:48.000 --> 00:45:51.250
the sufferings caused by a wounded environment,

00:45:51.310 --> 00:45:56.810
or the great promise that arises from a land that has been scarred.

00:46:06.430 --> 00:46:08.730
Only a few miles north of Lake Tongsap,

00:46:08.890 --> 00:46:11.940
a final mission within an forgotten era.

00:46:12.000 --> 00:46:19.310
The glory of Cambodia is, in its majority,

00:46:19.690 --> 00:46:21.410
forgotten in a distant past.

00:46:32.460 --> 00:46:34.840
A thousand years ago, where the jungle now invades,

00:46:35.140 --> 00:46:39.880
the city of Angkor was the center of power of the entire Asian Southwest,

00:46:39.880 --> 00:46:45.500
ruled by kings and gods who built an immense system of canals and temples,

00:46:45.680 --> 00:46:50.140
which continues to be the largest religious building ever made.

00:46:50.420 --> 00:46:56.600
But today, one of the wonders of universal architecture

00:46:56.600 --> 00:46:58.780
is ruined by the lack of conservation.

00:47:00.000 --> 00:47:01.180
the land is entangled in disorder.

00:47:01.600 --> 00:47:06.740
In Cambodia, even the antiques are victims of violence.

00:47:17.420 --> 00:47:21.700
In Vietnam, however, the conflict already appears as a scattered memory,

00:47:21.700 --> 00:47:25.740
even on the border of the Mekong Delta, in the city of Ho Chi Minh,

00:47:26.640 --> 00:47:28.180
the center of power of today's Southeast Asia.

00:47:32.520 --> 00:47:36.510
Here, prosperity arrives, bringing its own type of turbulence,

00:47:36.930 --> 00:47:39.420
a tide of modern objects,

00:47:39.420 --> 00:47:42.760
and the prospect of an invasion by foreign factories

00:47:42.760 --> 00:47:45.190
to employ the Vietnamese labor force.

00:47:45.350 --> 00:47:51.640
However, the American failure in interrupting the influx of products.

00:47:55.800 --> 00:47:59.960
40% of the nation had not yet been born when the war with America began.

00:48:00.000 --> 00:48:04.240
when the recovery, now bearing fruit, began.

00:48:05.020 --> 00:48:12.320
Their eyes do not see past sadness, but future wonders.

00:48:14.440 --> 00:48:21.620
Crucial changes may soon end the simple life of the people of the great Mekong.
